---
import comparison from '../../../data/neural-event-scientific-comparison.json';

const thresholdRule = comparison.comparisons.find((item) => item.model === 'threshold_candidate_rule')!;
const svm = comparison.comparisons.find((item) => item.model === 'three_class_svm')!;
const waveformModel = comparison.comparisons.find((item) => item.model === 'frozen_compact_model')!;
const percent = (value: number) => `${(value * 100).toFixed(1)}%`;
---

<section class="event-conclusion" aria-labelledby="conclusion-title">
  <header>
    <p>Conclusion</p>
    <div>
      <h2 id="conclusion-title">Multichannel morphology improves event classification</h2>
      <p>
        In repeated subject-grouped cross-validation, the waveform model achieved a macro F1 of
        {' '}{waveformModel.macro_f1.toFixed(3)} and {percent(waveformModel.accuracy)} accuracy.
        Under the same three-class labeling scheme, the threshold-based candidate rule reached
        a macro F1 of {thresholdRule.macro_f1.toFixed(3)} and {percent(thresholdRule.accuracy)} accuracy,
        while a direct three-class SVM achieved {svm.macro_f1.toFixed(3)} macro F1 and
        {' '}{percent(svm.accuracy)} accuracy. These comparisons suggest that the multichannel
        waveform contains discriminative structure that is not captured by fixed detection
        thresholds or a conventional classifier alone. Because all results come from internal
        cross-validation, performance still needs to be confirmed in an independent cohort.
      </p>
    </div>
  </header>

  <div class="future-work">
    <p>Further work</p>
    <ul>
      <li>Support a variable number of recording channels so predictions can use all available electrodes without requiring a fixed three-channel input.</li>
      <li>Move from classifying detected events to predicting ripple or IED occurrence from the neural activity in preceding time windows.</li>
    </ul>
  </div>
</section>

<style>
  .event-conclusion {
    margin: 0 0 var(--project-section-gap);
    padding: 28px 0 0;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--rule);
  }
  .event-conclusion header,
  .future-work {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 112px minmax(0, 1fr);
    gap: 28px;
  }
  .event-conclusion header > p,
  .future-work > p {
    margin: 3px 0 0;
    color: var(--muted);
    font-size: var(--project-label-size);
    text-transform: uppercase;
    letter-spacing: .06em;
  }
  .event-conclusion h2 {
    margin: 0;
    color: var(--text-strong);
    font-size: var(--project-heading-size);
    line-height: 1.3;
    font-weight: 400;
    letter-spacing: -.01em;
  }
  .event-conclusion header div > p {
    max-width: 620px;
    margin: 14px 0 0;
    color: var(--text);
    font-size: var(--project-body-size);
    line-height: var(--project-body-leading);
  }
  .future-work {
    margin-top: 28px;
    padding: 20px 0;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--subtle-rule);
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--rule);
  }
  .future-work ul { display: grid; gap: 10px; max-width: 590px; margin: 0; padding: 0; list-style: none; }
  .future-work li { position: relative; padding-left: 16px; color: var(--text); font-size: var(--project-body-size); line-height: var(--project-body-leading); }
  .future-work li::before { content: '—'; position: absolute; left: 0; color: var(--faint); }

  @media (max-width: 620px) {
    .event-conclusion header,
    .future-work { grid-template-columns: 1fr; gap: 12px; }
    .event-conclusion h2 { font-size: var(--project-heading-size); }
  }
</style>
